## Repository evidence

What the Quick Scan found, each item with the path that proves it. Facts the code
already answers never became questions.

## Domain interpretation

The business domain, its terminology, and how the goal reads inside it. Omit this
section when the goal is purely technical and local.

## Questions and answers

| ID | Question | Answer | Decision |
|----|----------|--------|----------|

One row per answered question. The decision column records what the answer changed.

## Automatic decisions

Reversible technical mechanics resolved under Recommendation Authority, with the
reason each one was clearly safer and simpler. These did not consume the question
budget.

## Consensus

The brainstorm result: agreed facts, live inferences, and the disagreements that
mattered. Record what the reviewers disagreed on and how it resolved, not the
conversation.

## Open risks

Anything unresolved that the specification must account for.
